            {
                "entry_id": "848508e2-6511-3798-a55d-ae30a1eb49e4",
                "word": "boomer",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "1cb73d5c-47db-4db2-ba3e-b82fd8690915",
                        "entry_id": "848508e2-6511-3798-a55d-ae30a1eb49e4",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "boomers"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e09fc030-1dad-3785-b704-5df26690948f",
                        "entry_id": "848508e2-6511-3798-a55d-ae30a1eb49e4",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Ellipsis of baby boomer."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "abbreviation",
                            "alt-of",
                            "ellipsis",
                            "informal"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "805c8132-2792-4a3f-956e-adc7dbc24a24",
                                "sense_id": "e09fc030-1dad-3785-b704-5df26690948f",
                                "text": "Boomers came of age in the era of the Beatles and Led Zeppelin."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "fa625cbd-703e-4537-98bd-9dab7e093a53",
                                "sense_id": "e09fc030-1dad-3785-b704-5df26690948f",
                                "text": "To the many Boomers who sensed that something had gone awry in Greatest Generation America, Mad was a glimmer of truth, a benign but trenchant voice against hypocrisy and pretense, a way to laugh at parents who fretted over status symbols and authorities who talked one way but acted another."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ca61009e-fc16-462b-8053-242f2be5465f",
                                "sense_id": "e09fc030-1dad-3785-b704-5df26690948f",
                                "text": "These fears have been exacerbated by the recession, which forced many boomers to turn to Social Security earlier than anticipated because of long-term unemployment and financial crises (Johnson and Wilson, 2010a, b)."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "09db68aa-f976-39aa-82c7-c159251a2967",
                        "entry_id": "848508e2-6511-3798-a55d-ae30a1eb49e4",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An elderly person, regardless of generation."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "broadly",
                            "derogatory",
                            "slang",
                            "sometimes"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "6804fe0a-78e3-4ac3-988d-45c40506c3f3",
                                "sense_id": "09db68aa-f976-39aa-82c7-c159251a2967",
                                "text": "I'm going to be a boomer by the time this thing is over."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "aea553f2-babe-3c0a-8af3-4d40a4f130fb",
                        "entry_id": "848508e2-6511-3798-a55d-ae30a1eb49e4",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A person who is too old to be familiar with the use of recent technology."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "broadly",
                            "derogatory",
                            "slang",
                            "sometimes"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e5578a3e-e55b-49ee-a2b6-c88aec4ba89e",
                                "sense_id": "aea553f2-babe-3c0a-8af3-4d40a4f130fb",
                                "text": "I'm such a boomer; I have no idea how to use this phone."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
            {
                "entry_id": "b1dd7831-4853-3863-b341-73a7c9742c9e",
                "word": "Boomer",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "99922a40-af34-43eb-949c-e2a658193ab0",
                        "entry_id": "b1dd7831-4853-3863-b341-73a7c9742c9e",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "Boomers"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "dc563ae4-c7d8-3e41-80f0-620a39a16107",
                        "entry_id": "b1dd7831-4853-3863-b341-73a7c9742c9e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A member of a 19th century movement which campaigned for the opening of \\\"Unassigned Lands\\\" within the Indian Territory (now Oklahoma) for settlement."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "US",
                            "historical"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "23d5cc6b-18a7-4e38-81f0-57dab9b1b159",
                                "sense_id": "dc563ae4-c7d8-3e41-80f0-620a39a16107",
                                "text": "Some skunk of a Sooner, sneaking in ahead of the Run, had set the blaze to keep the Boomers off, saving the land for himself."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "68cc7961-06ca-308c-b391-240ef260b8d5",
                        "entry_id": "b1dd7831-4853-3863-b341-73a7c9742c9e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Alternative form of boomer (“baby boomer”)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "alt-of",
                            "alternative"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "4a0e8e28-00bd-44d0-bd2f-f44fd63231aa",
                                "sense_id": "68cc7961-06ca-308c-b391-240ef260b8d5",
                                "text": "Someday, Boomers hope, Millennials will build according to great ideals their parents can only envision, act on vital issues their parents can only ponder."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "cd08406c-3209-4812-a772-6a34f3486b69",
                                "sense_id": "68cc7961-06ca-308c-b391-240ef260b8d5",
                                "text": "In a somewhat bizarre set of survey data from 2015, 33 percent of Millennials identified as Gen X, and 8 percent said that they were Boomers. Fifteen percent of Gen Xers said that they identified as Boomers, while a baffled 2 percent of Boomers and 4 percent of Silents thought of themselves as Millennials."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e2d13ca5-bad4-4a4b-8431-321537385c31",
                                "sense_id": "68cc7961-06ca-308c-b391-240ef260b8d5",
                                "text": "Back in the 80s he [Ben Elton] was one of the angry young things of alternative comedy, but this time he was hosting up-and-coming acts. ‘It just goes to show that Boomers and Generation Zedders can get on after all!’"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            }
        ],
